There are lots of way of defining callables. Some work but have inconsistent behaviours.

Currently, there are some forms of creating callables that are not consistent when it is used:

{code}
$callable = "self::method";
$callable = "parent::method";
$callable = "static::method";
$callable = ["self", "method"];
$callable = ["parent", "method"];
$callable = ["static", "method"];
$callable = ["MyClass", "MyParentClass::myMethod"];
$callable = [new MyClass(), "MyOtherClass::myMethod"];
{code}

https://php.watch/versions/8.2/partially-supported-callable-deprecation

These typically have a reference to:
* self
* parent
* static
* A parent method

I'm not sure how we will find all of these.

Supported string interpolations:
{code}
$name = 'PHP';
echo "Hello $name"; // Hello PHP
echo "Hello {$name}"; // Hello PHP
{code}

The following will no longer be supported:
{code}
$name = 'PHP';
$var = 'name';
echo "Hello ${name}"; // Dollar outside of curly braces deprecated
echo "Hello $$var"; // Variable variables deprecated
echo "Hello ${$var}"; // Variable variables deprecated
echo "Hello $$object->getMethod()"; // Variable expressions deprecated
{code}

The following can be used instead:
{code}
echo "Hello {$name}"; // Dollar moved inside the braces
echo "Hello {$$var}"; // Variable variables can be used inside braces
echo "Hello {${$object->getMethod()}}"; // Variable expressions can be used inside braces
{code}

https://php.watch/versions/8.2/$%7Bvar%7D-string-interpolation-deprecated

Note: This is the _opposite_ of JavaScript.

https://php.watch/versions/8.2/mbstring-qprint-base64-uuencode-html-entities-deprecated

The mbstring extension has deprecated conversion to and from:
* BASE64
* UUENCODE
* HTML-ENTITIES (aliased to html)
* Quoted-Printable (aliased to qprint)

These all have existing functions which can just be used, for example:
{code}
- $base64Encoded = mb_convert_encoding('test', 'Base64'));
+ $base64Encoded = base64_encode('test'));
{code}

Just run:

{code}
composer require --dev php-parallel-lint/php-parallel-lint && \
vendor/bin/parallel-lint --show-deprecated --exclude 'vendor' .
{code}

And fix all the problems detected by the linter

